# 🧠 Set Operators — Key Takeaway

| Operator | Business Meaning | Result |
|---|---|---|
| `UNION` | Combine both customer lists and remove duplicates | Unique customers |
| `UNION ALL` | Combine both customer lists and retain duplicates | All records |
| `INTERSECT` | Find customers present in both channels | Common customers |
| `EXCEPT` | Find customers present in Online but not Store | Online-only customers |

### Simple Mental Model

```text
UNION
A + B
→ Everything from both
→ Duplicates removed


UNION ALL
A + B
→ Everything from both
→ Duplicates retained


INTERSECT
A ∩ B
→ Only common records


EXCEPT
A - B
→ Records in A but not in B
